WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.440
- Have a seat.

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.810
- Thank you for being here.

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.459
- Y'all sharp, y'all sharp.

00:00:04.459 --> 00:00:05.408
Why y'all look so good.

00:00:05.408 --> 00:00:07.830
- I'm just saying we do
have a certain earthy tone

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.030
going today.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.220
I haven't seen you since New
York and y'all know each other.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.053
Y'all go way back.

00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:12.886
- Yes, yes, yes.

00:00:12.886 --> 00:00:13.740
- [Kelly] How do y'all know each other?

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.720
- We, well bumped into
each other a ton and then

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.030
I begged Karamo to come
do a podcast for me.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.530
And it was the best episode
of the whole podcast.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.430
- Aw, thank you brother.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.263
I would do anything for him.

00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:22.096
He's such a great guy.

00:00:22.096 --> 00:00:24.570
All he does is just give, give,
give when he's not working.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:25.440
- Oh my gosh well-

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.000
- That's like you.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.230
- I do like to work a lot.

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.063
I know.

00:00:29.063 --> 00:00:29.896
I probably need to go on your show

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:30.729
and you need to talk to me about that.

00:00:30.729 --> 00:00:31.562
(Karamo laughs)

00:00:31.562 --> 00:00:32.940
So wait, so you say that you haven't

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.470
had a cookie cutter
life, so what do you...

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.240
that means something
different for everybody

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.610
- Well, I am a talk show guest.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.500
So like, the way I even found about my son

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.988
like I got papers on my doorstep
when he was 10 years old.

00:00:42.988 --> 00:00:43.821
- [Kelly] You told me yeah.

00:00:43.821 --> 00:00:44.654
- Yes, you know what I mean?

00:00:44.654 --> 00:00:46.860
Like, there was abuse in
my household growing up.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.080
You know, my father was
abusive to my mother.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.327
You know, there was drug
addiction, you know.

00:00:51.327 --> 00:00:53.160
And my son just recently came on my show.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.210
He was a addicted to drugs.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.650
I didn't know as a parent,

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.390
and I thought it had
skipped the generation.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.480
So I understand what people go through

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.340
and I'm vulnerable enough
to talk about my own life so

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.320
that people know I get
what you're going through

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.280
and I can help you solve it.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.350
'Cause I got the training
to solve it, you know?

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.646
- Well and I think too, I feel like-

00:01:08.646 --> 00:01:11.130
(audience clapping)

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:13.020
If we're gonna be put to
the test and have to go

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.433
through all this stuff,
you might as well use it.

00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:15.266
- [Karamo] Amen.

00:01:15.266 --> 00:01:16.099
- You know what I'm saying?

00:01:16.099 --> 00:01:17.820
And you have this
experience that is negative

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.170
and trying to make it a positive.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.760
I think that's what you're doing.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.190
And you hadn't started the show
yet, like whenever you came

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:24.810
on the show in New York,
so now you've started it.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:25.710
How much do you love it?

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:26.910
- I love it so much,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.281
but girl it so much work!

00:01:28.281 --> 00:01:29.114
- It is!

00:01:29.114 --> 00:01:30.180
It is a lot of work.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.013
- Date?

00:01:31.013 --> 00:01:31.894
Oh my gosh I was like,

00:01:31.894 --> 00:01:32.727
"Woooo!"

00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:34.110
This is a lot.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.062
- It is a lot of work, but I feel-

00:01:35.062 --> 00:01:36.210
- [Karamo] But it's rewarding.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.160
- It is rewarding and I
think it's really important.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.370
I feel like you seem to put
a lot of yourself into it.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:42.360
Like you've like,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.860
and what I say is your experience

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.570
and like you're relatable
and that's how you connect.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:46.403
I like that.

00:01:46.403 --> 00:01:47.236
- Thank you, I appreciate that.

00:01:47.236 --> 00:01:48.069
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:48.069 --> 00:01:48.902
- Well, I mean, my only goal for this show

00:01:48.902 --> 00:01:50.550
was to be able to help
people day in and day out.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.980
If a guest leaves my show and doesn't feel

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.380
as if I gave them some tools to be better

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.090
or that they felt more healed,

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.700
I literally have given like
five guests my telephone number

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:00.870
and been like, "Hey,"

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.070
and then I make sure.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.200
Or we've had only like a couple times

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.700
and I brought them back because like,

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:06.690
my goal is to heal.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.790
I'm so tired of us as human beings

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:10.200
feeling in pain

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.700
and feeling like we're alone

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.500
and feeling like no one understands.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.460
And I'm just like,

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:15.570
we have to be better

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.040
and someone has to give us the tools.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.060
Like if I could go back

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.190
and restructure the
American school system,

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:21.300
I would do so many things different

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.500
because I think some of the things-

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.330
- One, implement mental health.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:25.380
- Implement mental health,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.210
because you see kids being bullied

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.760
feeling sad, feeling alone.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.030
And even the most "popular
kids" have these feelings

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.760
of inadequacy and feeling
like "I'm not enough."

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.050
And it just turns into adults.

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:37.883
You see that,

00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:38.970
that young boy in that clip

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:41.130
this is a young boy who's 24 as a parent.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.540
And I'm like trying to stop him

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.780
from becoming a 40 year old
parent that's not doing right.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.182
And I think like we should,
we all deserve to be

00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:51.030
in good environments and be
around people that we love

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.230
and feel supportive,

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.910
but someone has to teach us.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.721
- And I also think though
that society kind of-

00:02:55.721 --> 00:02:56.554
(audience clapping)

00:02:56.554 --> 00:02:57.740
- Yeah absolutely.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.460
I also think too like,

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.900
don't you think they...

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.090
People tell us even from when we're kids

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.310
like, you know, you gotta be happy.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:06.420
And it's like, "Well what?"

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.250
Everybody's not happy all the time.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.450
Like and that's not,

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.640
that's not even doable.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.160
Like you can't possibly accomplish that.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.260
And I think it's, I
think it's more important

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.100
to teach someone that like,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.780
no, you're not gonna
be happy all the time.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:19.710
Life can be hard.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:23.310
Like you gotta learn the
skill set to get through that.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.143
- Listen I-

00:03:24.143 --> 00:03:25.830
- To appreciate the happy
when it comes 'cause

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.090
it's not gonna be happy all the time.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.737
And I think we do a disservice
to kids by saying like,

00:03:29.737 --> 00:03:30.637
"Oh no, are you happy?"

00:03:30.637 --> 00:03:31.650
"I want you to be happy."

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:32.970
And it's just like happy, happy, happy.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:33.803
And it's like,

00:03:33.803 --> 00:03:34.636
you don't have to be happy all the time.

00:03:34.636 --> 00:03:35.469
- [Karamo] Yeah.

00:03:35.469 --> 00:03:36.302
- It's okay.

00:03:36.302 --> 00:03:37.980
- You know I wrote a book with my son

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.360
called "I'm Okay To Feel."

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.060
And literally the book is
about just exactly that.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.610
Telling kids it is okay to feel

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:45.443
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:45.443 --> 00:03:47.460
- Instead of that narrative
of being happy, happy, happy.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.690
Consistently, consistently.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:49.523
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:49.523 --> 00:03:50.356
- And it has worked.

00:03:50.356 --> 00:03:52.500
Like I go in these schools
and we do these readings

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.947
and kids will come up and be like,

00:03:53.947 --> 00:03:55.987
"For the first time, like I'm okay.

00:03:55.987 --> 00:03:57.390
"Like you're telling me I can say

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.100
that I'm sad, or I'm mad today,

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:00.660
And I'm not gonna get in trouble?"

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.000
Because sometimes I feel
like if someone says that,

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.290
they feel like they're being punished

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:05.277
and then we become
adults and we close off.

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:06.480
- [Kelly] Or there's
something wrong with them.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:07.470
- Something wrong with them.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.340
That's not, you know what I mean?

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.173
That's not okay.

00:04:09.173 --> 00:04:10.590
Especially as black, young black boys,

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:11.423
I don't know how you grew up

00:04:11.423 --> 00:04:14.130
but it was like, you don't talk about it.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:14.963
- Go do it.

00:04:14.963 --> 00:04:15.986
- [Karamo] Go do it.

00:04:15.986 --> 00:04:16.950
- What's the problem? Go do it.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:17.783
- What's the problem?

00:04:17.783 --> 00:04:18.843
And I'm like,

00:04:18.843 --> 00:04:20.340
the problem is I don't feel like it today.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.830
Can you listen to my feelings?

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:22.831
You know what I mean?

00:04:22.831 --> 00:04:23.664
And so, but-

00:04:23.664 --> 00:04:25.020
- I love this thing with
my three-year-old daughter

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.060
and she comes home from preschool

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.590
and she tells you her color.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.820
That's her feeling of the day.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:30.900
So they've equated like
a feeling to a color.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.066
- [Kelly] Oh, my kid does-

00:04:32.066 --> 00:04:32.899
- So she'll come home and she'll be like,

00:04:32.899 --> 00:04:34.067
"I'm yellow today Daddy."

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:35.024
(Karamo and Kelly laugh)

00:04:35.024 --> 00:04:35.857
- And I'm like

00:04:35.857 --> 00:04:37.801
"So where's the book with the colors?"

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:38.707
"What does yellow mean?"

00:04:38.707 --> 00:04:41.100
"How do I do yellow today?"

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:41.933
- Oh my god,

00:04:41.933 --> 00:04:43.350
so my daughter going to
bed last night just was

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:45.570
throwing a tantrum and I,

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.790
whatever for, I'm sure it mattered

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.427
but like, it didn't,
it was like something,

00:04:49.427 --> 00:04:50.700
it was just something dumb.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:51.660
She didn't wanna sleep by herself.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:52.493
Whatever.

00:04:52.493 --> 00:04:53.970
One of her friends gets to
sleep with her mom all the time.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.013
And I'm like, "You're not
in my bed on the time."

00:04:55.013 --> 00:04:55.846
- Yeah, not happening.

00:04:55.846 --> 00:04:56.679
- So build a bridge.

00:04:56.679 --> 00:04:58.263
And anyway, so I told her, I was like all,

00:04:58.263 --> 00:05:00.180
you know, all therapy about it.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.013
I was like,

00:05:01.013 --> 00:05:01.920
"Oh my gosh, you know what?

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:02.880
I want you to feel this,

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:03.750
you're sad about it,

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:06.180
and you can cry about it,
but like, I'm gonna go."

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.140
- Yes, I'm gonna go.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.053
- [Kelly] Like I'm going.

00:05:08.053 --> 00:05:08.886
- Yes.

00:05:08.886 --> 00:05:10.297
- And you are allowed to
sit here in your feelings.

00:05:10.297 --> 00:05:11.280
- [Karamo] Yes, be in it!

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.621
- You were allowed to feel yellow.

00:05:12.621 --> 00:05:13.454
- Yes.

00:05:13.454 --> 00:05:16.148
- I'm going to feel green
and I'm going to go.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:17.521
(everyone laughs)

00:05:17.521 --> 00:05:18.354
- I'm gonna tell you something.

00:05:18.354 --> 00:05:19.187
- [Kelly] Go for it.

00:05:19.187 --> 00:05:20.020
- You did good.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:20.853
- Okay.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:21.686
- Because what you did is you actually

00:05:21.686 --> 00:05:23.070
also modeled a healthy boundary.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:25.380
So you, Mama Kelly you did it good!

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.788
Listen, you did it good!

00:05:26.788 --> 00:05:27.621
- Wait, wait.

00:05:27.621 --> 00:05:28.530
- Not only did he say,

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.270
You're allowed to feel
what you want to feel,

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.230
take the time you need,"

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.250
but then you were like,

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.660
Take your boundary girl.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.100
Good job mama.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.120
Listen, I don't think we encouraged

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:37.440
to say a good job to
our moms all the time.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.889
- You have no idea how hard
I've been working on boundaries.

00:05:40.889 --> 00:05:42.240
- You did good! You did good!

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.370
- I was like, thank you.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.533
I'm gonna celebrate tonight with a drink.

